on a snow-bound road west of Kiev where  months earlier Russian tanks had rolled  war crimes investigators from Ukraine's  Center for civil liberties are following  in their tracks in an old Honda Jazz  they've come to the Village of makariv  to record the testimony of a woman who  says her husband was killed by the  Russians  and here is where Alexi died from what I  know he was struck with something sharp  like the handle of a knife or a rifle  stock behind his left ear then they  brought him here and killed him five  stab wounds to the chest her mobile  phone contains a wealth of evidence her  descriptions are Stark and matter of  fact  here is where his best friend Andre was  shot in the head this is what was left  after his body was retrieved I have many  photos  and Alexi's body was here to be honest I  have no idea who put his body in the  boot of the car here you can see the  spot we are standing where the car was  parked  it's a painstaking business collecting  evidence of alleged war crimes like this  a process repeated already thousands of  times and there may well be thousands  more and they don't even know for sure  whether these crimes will ever be  prosecuted there is no International  tribunal yet at which to try them our  website is a Tribunal for Putin and it's  our database of war crimes so you can  see the number of  incident Moro 25  000.  certainly this is a process that will  take time however we must collect this  information so nothing gets lost are you  confident that these crimes will be  brought to Justice  yes I'm confident Justice will happen  Justice may be slow but the certainty is  reassuring for this Widow of the war and  many like her Jonah Al Jazeera makariv  Ukraine
 

